# Report

`jev_report.py` writes an HTML page from files judge-jev already wrote. It never calls Jev, so it needs no key and no consent. It renders with the `sc-compose` CLI, which must be on PATH.

```bash
R="<this skill's directory>/scripts/jev_report.py"
```

## Quality report: one fix run

A quality report covers one fix run (`references/fix-strategy.md`): one record, from the author's text (`base`) to the text you are handing back (`final`). It reads the run's workspace, not the log, so runs from other loops never mix in. Run it from the repository root after the drift review:

```bash
. .sc/judge-jev/fix/<ID>/env
uv run -q --script "$R" quality --fix-dir "$W" --review "$W/review.json" --out .sc/judge-jev/reports --name "$ID"
```

From the workspace it reads `env` (`ID`, `KIND`, `F`), every `<step>-r<N>.json` (the `quality` output of run N of step `base`, `c1`, `comb`, `final`, ...), `original.md`, `current.md` and each candidate's `<step>.md`. Without a `final` step the page compares `base` with the latest step and says so.

The page shows, in order:

- **What improved and why.** One row per statement a rule fired on (an ADR's whole-record wave is one row): in how many runs it fired in `base` and in `final`, the outcome (`fixed`, `improved`, `still fails`, `regressed`), the answers that explain it (Jev's choice, its confidence, how many runs chose it, and the criterion; the base answers are taken from the runs it fired in) and the candidate steps that cleared it on their own.
- **Confidence.** One tab per question; one row per statement; a hollow dot per `base` run, a solid dot per `final` run; red is a Fix answer (its criterion carries `Fix:`). The dashed lines are the threshold (0.6) and the noise boundary (0.5). A Fix answer can remain in a passing run: the verdict comes from the tree's rules.
- **Steps.** Each step's verdict tally (`no 3/3`, `yes 6/6`), the statements it fires on and those it clears against `base`. A run file that holds an error envelope counts as an error, not a verdict.
- **Text.** The diff of the record's own section (from its heading to the next heading of the same level) from `original.md` to `current.md`, rendered as Markdown: removed text struck in red, added text in green. "Changes only" shows the changed blocks with one block of context; "Whole document" shows the full section. Each candidate's edit to `original.md` is listed below it.
- Your **drift review**, if you passed one, and every run.

The page is PASS when every `final` run is `yes`.

### Drift review file

`--review` takes your drift review (`references/fix-strategy.md` step 8) as JSON. One entry per change you kept or reverted:

```json
{
  "reviewed_at": "2026-11-10",
  "kept": [{"change": "defined 'profile'", "why": "covers every use in the record", "authority": "docs/cli.md:79"}],
  "discarded": [{"change": "dropped 'for the same file'", "why": "narrowed the scope", "authority": "REQ-ABC-0001 original"}]
}
```

`change` and `why` are required; `authority` names the record, file and line the change aligns with or drifts from. A file off this shape is `VALIDATION.INPUT`, naming each bad field.

## Check report

judge-jev has no `check` command yet (SKILL.md: compliance mode is not in this release). `jev_report.py check` renders the results contract that command will print, so the report exists when the command does:

```bash
uv run -q --script "$R" check --results check-results.json --out .sc/judge-jev/reports
```

```json
{
  "run": "c1",
  "questions": "",
  "pairs": [
    {"record_id": "REQ-ABC-0001", "record_kind": "req", "record_title": "Exit codes",
     "location": "templates/dev.md.j2", "mode": "task",
     "requests": [
       {"variant": "raw", "request_id": "c1/1", "verdict": "yes", "text": "<template>", "reason": []},
       {"variant": "rendered", "request_id": "c1/2", "verdict": "no", "text": "<assignment>", "reason": []}
     ]}
  ]
}
```

- `mode` is `prompt`, `skill`, `task` or `agent` (target class agent text) or `code` (target class code). `location` is `path`, `path#Heading` or `path::Symbol`.
- A `task` pair has two requests, `raw` then `rendered`; every other pair has one request with no `variant`.
- Each `reason` entry is one answer: `id`, `text`, `choice`, `confidence` and `criterion`, as `quality` reports them.
- A pair meets its record when every request's verdict is `yes`.

The page aggregates per record (met at every location, or the failing locations) and per location (the records it meets and fails), with one panel per location: the confidence chart (one tab per question, one row per record; in `task` mode the raw template hollow and the rendered assignment solid), each request's answers, and the text it sent.

## Output

`--out DIR` receives `<name>.html`, the sidecar `<name>.json` (the same data, for agents) and one XHTML panel per run or location in `<name>/`. `--name` defaults to `quality-report` or `check-report`. Each panel has Copy JSON and Copy Context buttons; Copy Context is a plain-text summary to paste into the next step.

Open the page and look at it before you report it. Report the path to the user with the pass counts it shows. Do not commit the report unless the user asks.

## Errors

One JSON envelope on stdout; exit 0 when the report was written, 2 with a typed error:

| Code | Cause | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `REPORT.NO_RUNS` | `--fix-dir` has no `env` file, or no `base-r<N>.json`. | Pass `.sc/judge-jev/fix/<ID>` after the loop's base step. |
| `VALIDATION.INPUT` | A bad argument, review file or check results file, or a run file of another record. | Fix the fields named in the message. |
| `DEPENDENCY.SC_COMPOSE` | `sc-compose` is not on PATH. | `references/installation-and-troubleshooting.md`. |
| `RENDER.FAILED` | sc-compose rejected a template or its variables. | Report it with the command line. |
| `SCRIPT.IO` | A file cannot be read or written. | Pass a readable input and a writable `--out`. |
